cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite Version 0.1.0 of this research repository."
title: "Sharp determinant bounds for three near-Hadamard families"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Kline
    given-names: Jeffery
repository-code: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/near-hadamard-determinant-bound"
url: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/near-hadamard-determinant-bound"
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  Momihara, Suda and Xiang built three families of +-1 matrices, Classes
  (4)-(6) of their Theorem 1.6, with orders n = q+1 for prime powers
  q = 1 mod 4. They asked whether each determinant is at least 0.8 times the
  Ehlich-Wojtas bound W_n = (2n-2)(n-2)^((n-2)/2) for every n >= 30 (the 0.8
  question of their Problem 7.1, which is Problem 15 of a 2026 survey). This
  paper proves that it is. In each family the ratio to W_n tends to
  sqrt(e)/2, and the smallest ratios over n >= 30 are about 0.8169, 0.8154
  and 0.8184, reached only at n = 30, 38 and 50. The proof uses two exact
  moment identities from character orthogonality and the size of a Gauss
  sum, with exact integer and ball-arithmetic certificates for the finite
  range. Novelty is unconfirmed: the full text of a 2026 paper by Li,
  Momihara and Xiang was not read.
keywords:
  - Hadamard matrices
  - maximal determinant
  - near-Hadamard matrices
  - Ehlich-Wojtas bound
  - Gauss sums
  - Jacobi sums
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Square (1,-1)-matrices with large determinants and near-Hadamard matrices"
    authors:
      - family-names: Momihara
        given-names: Koji
      - family-names: Suda
        given-names: Sho
      - family-names: Xiang
        given-names: Qing
    journal: "Linear Algebra and its Applications"
    volume: 654
    year: 2022
    doi: 10.1016/j.laa.2022.08.028
